Subject: telnet/sys_bsd.c: drop spurious arg to stilloob()

stilloob() is declared and defined as `int stilloob (void)` in
network.c / externs.h, but sys_bsd.c calls it with the socket fd as
an arg.  On most hosts the call site is shielded by an OOB-handling
branch the configure pass dead-codes out, so the arity mismatch
escapes notice; on substrate the branch compiles and the build
breaks.  Drop the extraneous argument.

---
diff -urN a/telnet/sys_bsd.c b/telnet/sys_bsd.c
--- a/telnet/sys_bsd.c
+++ b/telnet/sys_bsd.c
@@ -1235,7 +1235,7 @@
 		  c = recv (net, netiring.supply, canread, 0);
 		  if (clocks.didnetreceive < clocks.gotDM)
 		    {
-		      SYNCHing = stilloob (net);
+		      SYNCHing = stilloob ();
 		    }
 		}
 	      else if (first && c > 0)
